# The build context is `ci/`, and this narrows it to the one file the Dockerfile copies.
#
# Deny-by-default rather than a list of things to exclude. An exclusion list has to be updated every
# time the repository grows a directory worth keeping out of a build layer, and it is only ever
# updated by someone who thought of it.
#
# Belt to the build context's braces: `context: ci` already keeps the checkout out of reach, so a
# Dockerfile that says `COPY . /somewhere` gets this directory rather than the repository. This file
# makes that "gets entrypoint.sh".
*
!entrypoint.sh
